.TH CBMAP_RESET 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cbmap_reset \- clear all elements from the map
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cbstmap.h>

ccol_retval_t cbmap_reset(cbmap cbm);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Removes all key-value pairs from the map using iterative post-order
traversal. The map becomes empty but remains usable.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
cbm  BST map to reset
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns ccol_success on success
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
O(n) complexity
All nodes are destroyed, keys and values freed
Map structure remains valid for reuse
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cbmap_destroy (3),
.BR cbmap_delete_elem (3)
